  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0cd0b2982be60c644a30780b118c3dc1, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The corner shop. Mum needed bread. I had the coupons the whole time.
    midDaysAnswer: Block A. Mum sent me for matches. The ash started, so I ran.
    finalDaysAnswer: Around the blocks. Mum isn't back yet. The flat is too quiet.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: From school. Lessons finished early today, so the teacher let us go.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: From home, in Block F. Second floor, next to the stairs.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The station. I met my dad. He got back from Varka yesterday.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My hands shake sometimes. Mum says it's the cold. No fever, I checked.
    midDaysAnswer: I can't sleep much. And I had a nosebleed. Is that bad? Sorry.
    finalDaysAnswer: My tummy hurts a lot. Maybe there isn't enough food. I'm fine. Mostly.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No. My hands are totally still, look. I never get nervous about anything.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. I sleep really well. Mum and Dad tuck me in every night.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I'm fine. The school nurse checked me this morning before lessons.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Sorry, is this the right form? I filled it out twice just in case.
    - My hands keep shaking. It is probably just the cold, right?
    midDays:
    - Have you heard anything about Varka? My dad is there for work.
    - "Is it taking longer today? I don't mind, I'm just\u2026 checking."
    finalDays:
    - Do you think it still matters? Coming through here. I keep doing it anyway.
    - "Is there somewhere safer than this? Just\u2026 anywhere. I'm asking everyone."
